  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q25-task",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Mary leaves home and travels $10\\text{ km}$ due south and then $5\\text{ km}$ due east to go to school. Give true bearings correct to the nearest degree, using three digits.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the bearing of Mary’s school from home?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$153^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Let $\\alpha$ be the angle east of south from home to school.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac{5}{10}\\\\\\alpha&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{10}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing}&=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{10}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing}&\\approx153^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bearing is $153^\\circ$, to the nearest degree.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the bearing of Mary’s home from school?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$333^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Use the unrounded bearing from part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Reverse bearing}&=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{10}\\right)+180^\\circ\\\\\\text{Reverse bearing}&=360^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{10}\\right)\\\\\\text{Reverse bearing}&\\approx333^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bearing is $333^\\circ$, to the nearest degree.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
